Date: Sun, 12 Apr 2026 13:45:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 048/110] fix(nudge): normalize trailing slash in nudge targets
 (#3591)

* Add rig add API endpoint and whitelist for enclave dashboard

- Add `rig add` to AllowedCommands whitelist (with confirmation required)
- Add /api/rig/add endpoint that supports local bare repo creation
  for use within Nitro Enclaves where GitHub access is not available
- Local repo flow: mkdir + git init --bare + clone + initial commit + push
- Invalidate options cache after rig creation so rig list updates

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix(nudge): normalize trailing slash in nudge targets

The mail system uses "mayor/" and "deacon/" as canonical addresses, but
runNudge's role shortcut check expects bare names ("mayor", "deacon").
When the refinery engineer sends `gt nudge "mayor/" ...`, the trailing
slash causes it to bypass the role shortcut and hit parseAddress, which
splits "mayor/" into ["mayor", ""] and rejects the empty second
component. This silently drops all refinery-to-mayor nudges (post-merge,
branch-missing, merge-failure notifications).

Fix: TrimSuffix the trailing "/" early in runNudge before role resolution.

Also fixes pre-existing build error in compact_report_test.go
(wispTypeToCategory signature gained a second parameter).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

